rule: session-map
why: RULES.md rule 7 requires each of the three lines to name a .jsonl file whose base name matches a .jsonl file under the submission directory; all three here do, so the brief's session map (three entries) is satisfied.
expect: pass
file: submission/planning.jsonl
| {"type":"user","text":"decompose the routing console"}
file: submission/correction.jsonl
| {"type":"user","text":"the retry plan is wrong, stop"}
file: submission/testing.jsonl
| {"type":"user","text":"run the tests and report"}
file: SUBMISSION.md
| Session map:
| - Initial planning or decomposition: planning.jsonl, from the first message to the task list
| - Most important correction or change of direction: correction.jsonl, where the retry plan is rejected
| - Final testing and verification: testing.jsonl, the last 40 messages
